* Precision reference subsystem using ADR1399H and LTC6078
* Primary input node: IN (15V supply)
* Primary output node: OUT (7.05V buffered reference)

* 15V DC Supply
V1 IN 0 15

* Zener Bias Resistor (Targeting ~3mA: (15V - 7.05V) / 2.67k = 2.97mA)
R1 IN Z_node 2.67k

* ADR1399H Subcircuit
* Pin order (typical for LM399/ADR1399): Zener+, Zener-, Heater+, Heater-
X1 Z_node 0 IN 0 ADR1399H

* LTC6078 Op-Amp Buffer (Unity Gain Configuration)
* Pin order: IN+, IN-, V+, V-, OUT
X2 Z_node OUT IN 0 OUT LTC6078

* 1k Load on the output
Rload OUT 0 1k

* Load the manufacturer's library for the ADR1399H
.lib ADR1399H.sub

* Transient analysis to allow the heater thermal model and output to settle
.tran 1

.end
